    "scope": "Four actually inspected exterior photographs plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. No bespoke survey sources or redistributed pictures.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clocher_saint-Sacerdos_Sarlat.jpg",
        "author": "Jebulon",
        "date": "2011-08-05",
        "license": "CC0-1.0",
        "observed": "Inspected narrow-street tower view: golden ashlar square body with blind round arches, triple middle lights, paired tall louvered belfry lights, flared square slate roof, pinched upper bulb and little open lantern/weather vane. Foreground houses conceal the porch and nave."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarlat_-_Ancienne_cath%C3%A9drale_Saint-Sacerdos_-_PA00082916_-_011.jpg",
        "author": "Thesupermat",
        "date": "2012-04-16",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Inspected broader square/street view: the same layered stone tower, dark blue-grey roof and open lantern behind foreground houses. This is not a full nave view and supplies no exact dimensions."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint-Sacerdos_de_Sarlat_-_Vue_du_Chevet.JPG",
        "author": "Xfigpower",
        "date": "2013-04-27",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged choir view: high polygonal golden-stone choir with tall pointed stained-glass windows; lower radiating chapels with shallow dark tile/slate roofs and pointed lights; flying buttress arches and sparse finials; corner round stair turret with small conical roof/slits. Slate nave roof and bulb tower behind. Terrain and hidden roof joins are partly occluded."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarlat-la-Can%C3%A9da_-_Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint-Sacerdos_-_Clocher-porche_-4.jpg",
        "author": "MOSSOT",
        "date": "2003-07-14",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected tower-porch base: deep rectangular timber portal with pale jambs and projecting lintel, small round oculus, large blind round-arch body and small white clock dial partway up the blank front stage. Corner figure niches and side pointed window are simplified. Upper roof is cropped."
      }
    ]
